<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />

  <title>PRMS Score — Metabolic Performance Evaluation</title>
  <meta name="description" content="PRMS Score is the quantitative evaluation framework developed by PRMS Architecture Lab to assess metabolic performance in buildings through energy, water, comfort, resilience, carbon, economy, waste, and operational data." />

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css" />
</head>

<body>

<nav id="main-nav"></nav>

<main>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="hero-label">Evaluation Framework</p>
      <h1>PRMS Score<br><em>Metabolic Performance Evaluation</em></h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        PRMS Score is a quantitative evaluation framework developed by PRMS Architecture Lab
        to assess the integral metabolic performance of buildings through measurable indicators,
        weighted dimensions, verification levels, and operational data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <div>
        <h2>What PRMS Score measures</h2>
        <p>
          PRMS Score evaluates buildings as metabolic systems. Instead of assessing architecture
          only by form, function, or efficiency, it measures how a project produces, consumes,
          stores, reuses, verifies, and manages critical flows over time.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h3>Core purpose</h3>
        <p>
          To provide a measurable, comparable, and verifiable performance score for residential
          and small-scale architectural systems.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section muted">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>The 8 PRMS Score Dimensions</h2>

      <div class="grid-4">
        <div class="card"><h3>D1 · Energy</h3><p>Production, consumption, autonomy, and energy intensity.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>D2 · Water</h3><p>Rainwater capture, efficient use, reuse, and demand reduction.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>D3 · Waste</h3><p>Reduction, separation, recovery, and circularity potential.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>D4 · Comfort</h3><p>Thermal, lighting, acoustic, and indoor air quality performance.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>D5 · Economy</h3><p>Return on investment, payback, operating cost reduction, and value creation.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>D6 · Resilience</h3><p>Operational continuity under scarcity, outages, and extreme conditions.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>D7 · Carbon</h3><p>Operational emissions, avoided emissions, and net carbon balance.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>D8 · Operation & Data</h3><p>Monitoring, maintenance, data traceability, and intelligent management.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <div>
        <h2>Certification scale</h2>
        <p>
          The global score ranges from 0 to 100 and classifies each project into a metabolic
          performance level.
        </p>

        <table>
          <tr><th>Level</th><th>Score</th></tr>
          <tr><td>Metabolic Elite</td><td>90–100</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Metabolic Advanced</td><td>75–89</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Metabolic Standard</td><td>55–74</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Metabolic Basic</td><td>35–54</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Not Certified</td><td>0–34</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>Factor C</h2>
        <p>
          PRMS Score includes a confidence multiplier called Factor C. This factor adjusts the
          final score according to the reliability of the evidence used in the evaluation.
        </p>

        <table>
          <tr><th>Level</th><th>Evidence</th><th>Factor</th></tr>
          <tr><td>A</td><td>Verified continuous IoT data</td><td>1.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td>B</td><td>Official bills or utility meters</td><td>0.80</td></tr>
          <tr><td>C</td><td>Estimated declaration</td><td>0.40</td></tr>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="hero-label">Standard Reference</p>
      <h2>PRMS-SCORE-STD-2026-001</h2>
      <p>
        PRMS Score is documented as part of the PRMS research programme and is under development
        as a measurable standard for evaluating metabolic performance in housing and small-scale
        architectural systems.
      </p>

      <a class="button" href="/publications">View Research Publications</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href="/score/calculator">Open Calculator</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

<script src="/nav.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
